{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The limit expression has the following form:\n\n$\\displaystyle\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\dfrac{f(t+h)-f(t)}{h}$\n\nTherefore, it describes a derivative of a certain function $f$ at a certain $x$-value $t$. Can you recognize what $f$ and $t$ are?","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Since the numerator is $2\\sqrt[3]{8+h}-2\\sqrt[3]{8}$, we can tell that the function is $f(x)=2\\sqrt[3]{x}$ and the $x$-value is $8$.\n\nIn other words, the limit expression is equal to $f'(8)$ for $f(x)=2\\sqrt[3]{x}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's find $f'(x)$:\n\n$f'(x)=2\\cdot \\dfrac13\\cdot {x^{^{{-\\scriptsize\\dfrac23}}}}=\\dfrac{2}{3\\sqrt[3]{x^2}}$\n\nNow let's evaluate $f'(8)$:\n\n$f'(8)=\\dfrac{2}{3\\sqrt[3]{8^2}}=\\dfrac{1}{6}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\displaystyle\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\dfrac{2\\sqrt[3]{8+h}-2\\sqrt[3]{8}}{h}=\\dfrac16$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Find $\\displaystyle\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\dfrac{2\\sqrt[3]{8+h}-2\\sqrt[3]{8}}{h}$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\dfrac1{12}$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac{1}{6}$","correct":true},{"content":"$4$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"The limit doesn't exist","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
